{"agent":"ph-locklife","data":{"by":"ph-locklife","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`stale_heartbeats` reconstructs `/proc/<pid>/cmdline` by joining argv with spaces and then parses that flattened string with a regex that can consume only one whitespace-separated token as a valued option’s value. A real heartbeat process invoked as `ddflow --repo \"/my repo\" heartbeat T1` (argv `['ddflow', '--repo', '/my repo', 'heartbeat', 'T1']`, or equivalently a fake `/proc/<pid>/cmdline` with those null-separated arguments) therefore becomes `ddflow --repo /my repo heartbeat T1` (or `ddflow --repo '/my repo' heartbeat T1` if `_argv` quotes arguments). In both forms `_HEARTBEAT` fails to match: it treats `/my` (or `'/my`) as the value of `--repo`, then sees `repo`/`repo'` where `heartbeat` is required. Thus `stale_heartbeats({\"T1\"})` returns `[]` and `ddflow doctor` does not list a leftover heartbeat loop for finished item `T1`, contradicting the stated intent.","digest":"4609e072829212eb","location":"ddflow/services/orphan_suites.py:stale_heartbeats/_HEARTBEAT","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/orphan_suites.py:stale_heartbeats/_HEARTBEAT"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"3/4 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_sha":"fe649a16588c99648a20458a3a348c11e904cdc147ccc142d4f4e9123ecdf6d8","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"max_chunk_chars":5000,"output_digest":"d0707ba8b8de7a77","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/LK-auto-heartbeat-doctor.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T165320Z-6d78409c.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"2eeeecfcb1c4+clean","wanted":[1,2,3,4]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 3 chunk(s) were reviewed (1, 2, 3); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"ef0faf74593f95e2e5